<p class="kicker">HFT Practice · Lesson 0037 · Operator's Guide</p>
<h1>Using the Platform: From Fresh Clone to a Running Strategy Arena</h1>
<div class="why"><strong>Why this matters:</strong> the platform now has ~15 entry
points and a multi-stage workflow (train → validate → screen → live paper-trade →
monitor → decide). This is the map: what to run, in what order, and which safety
rails are watching you. Everything here is a real command from
<code>pyproject.toml</code>'s <code>[project.scripts]</code>.</div>

<div class="warn"><strong>Branch note:</strong> the arena commands
(<code>arena-run</code> and friends) live on the PR stack
<code>#52 → #53 → #63</code>. Until those merge to <code>main</code>, run them from
the <code>feature/july6-batch</code> branch.</div>

<h2 id="s1">1 · One-time setup</h2>
<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/bjl14710/algo_trading_practice.git
cd algo_trading_practice
uv sync --extra dev        <span class="cm"># installs everything + pytest; NEVER bare pip</span>
uv run pytest tests/ -m "not exercise"   <span class="cm"># sanity: should be all green</span></code></pre>
<p>Environment variables (only needed for their feature): <code>ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY</code>
(news pipeline), <code>WEB_AUTH_USER/PASS</code> (web app), <code>RH_USERNAME/PASSWORD/MFA</code>
(Robinhood execution). Docker users: <code>cp .env.docker.example .env.docker</code>, fill it,
never commit it.</p>

<h2 id="s2">2 · The command map</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th><th>When you run it</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>paper-backtest</code></td><td>Trains the GBM + historical backtest; <code>--save_model</code> writes the bundle (now with the drift reference baked in)</td><td>When (re)training a model</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>walkforward-sim</code></td><td>Rolling walk-forward with risk overlay; <code>--stress</code> replays COVID-2020 / 2022 / Q4-2018 shock windows</td><td>Validating a model before trusting it</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>arena-run backtest</code></td><td>Screens strategies (engulfing, technical, meanrev, gbm) through one filter bar; stores PASS/EXCLUDED + sizing mode + divergence fingerprint</td><td>Once per strategy configuration</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>arena-run live</code></td><td>One idempotent daily paper tick per PASS strategy — backfills missed days, evaluates breaker + divergence</td><td>Daily (cron or morning routine)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>arena-run report</code></td><td>Unranked side-by-side table: live vs backtest, win rate, drawdown, alerts</td><td>Whenever you want the standings</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>arena-run resume &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>The ONLY way to un-pause a breaker-tripped strategy</td><td>After you've reviewed why it tripped</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>arena-run ensemble</code></td><td>Weighted-vote meta-strategy from PASS members, weights = live Sharpe</td><td>Once members have ~20 live days</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>predict-next</code></td><td>Tomorrow's per-ticker predictions + allocation; <code>--explain</code> (SHAP), <code>--check_drift</code> (PSI)</td><td>Ad-hoc, or via morning-runner</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>analyze-equity</code></td><td>Sharpe/CAGR/drawdown from any equity CSV</td><td>After any backtest</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>web-hft</code> / <code>gui-hft</code></td><td>FastAPI web app (:8000) / Tkinter desktop GUI</td><td>Browsing results visually</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>rh-exec</code></td><td>Robinhood order submission — <strong>dry-run by default</strong></td><td>Only when you mean it</td></tr>
</table>

<h2 id="s3">3 · The core workflow, end to end</h2>
<h3>Step A — Train a model (optional: rule strategies need no model)</h3>
<pre><code>uv run paper-backtest --tickers_file tickers/sap500_tickers.txt \
    --start 2016-01-01 --end 2020-12-31 \
    --save_model models/my_bundle.joblib</code></pre>
<p>The bundle stores <code>{"model", "features", "feature_reference"}</code> — the
features list pins column order at inference (lesson 0035), the reference powers
drift checks (lesson 0036).</p>

<h3>Step B — Validate it, including against crashes</h3>
<pre><code>uv run walkforward-sim --model models/my_bundle.joblib \
    --start 2021-01-01 --end 2025-01-01 --stress
uv run analyze-equity --equity_csv walkforward_equity.csv</code></pre>
<p><code>--stress</code> appends one metrics row per historical shock window — the
scenarios a few months of live paper trading will never show you.</p>

<h3>Step C — Screen the arena field</h3>
<pre><code>uv run arena-run backtest --start 2023-01-01 --end 2025-01-01 \
    --tickers AAPL,MSFT,GOOG,AMZN,NVDA \
    --cost_model realistic          <span class="cm"># net-of-costs screening</span>
<span class="cm"># add gbm explicitly: --strategies engulfing,technical,meanrev,gbm --gbm_bundle models/my_bundle.joblib</span></code></pre>
<p>Each strategy gets PASS or EXCLUDED against a lenient bar (Sharpe &gt; 0, drawdown
&lt; 30%) — excluded ones stay visible in the report, never silently dropped. The
sizing mode chosen here (<code>conf_vol</code> by default) is locked to the strategy's
ledger from now on.</p>

<h3>Step D — Trade it live (paper), daily</h3>
<pre><code>uv run arena-run live      <span class="cm"># ticks every PASS strategy</span></code></pre>
<p>Idempotent: run it twice, nothing duplicates. Miss a week: it backfills
deterministically. Each tick also evaluates the drawdown breaker (auto-pause at
−20%) and the divergence z-test (flags likely overfits). Cron it or add it to your
morning routine next to <code>morning-runner</code>.</p>

<h3>Step E — Read the standings, act like the human in the loop</h3>
<pre><code>uv run arena-run report</code></pre>
<p>Key columns: <code>status</code> (PASS/EXCLUDED/PAUSED), <code>sharpe_divergence</code>
and <code>divergence_z</code> (overfit canaries), <code>vol_ratio</code>,
<code>paused_since</code>. A PAUSED strategy stays dark until
<code>arena-run resume &lt;name&gt;</code> — resuming resets its drawdown baseline to today.</p>

<h3>Step F — When track records exist, try the ensemble</h3>
<pre><code>uv run arena-run ensemble --name blend --members engulfing,technical,meanrev</code></pre>

<h2 id="s4">4 · The safety rails (what's protecting you)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Rail</th><th>Default</th><th>Override</th></tr>
<tr><td>Real-money orders</td><td><code>rh-exec</code> is dry-run</td><td><code>--no_dry_run</code>, typed by you, on purpose</td></tr>
<tr><td>Drawdown breaker</td><td>Pauses a live strategy at −20% from peak</td><td><code>--breaker_dd</code> / <code>--no_breaker</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Divergence alert</td><td>Flags (never pauses) at z &lt; −2 after 20 live days</td><td><code>--divergence_z</code>, <code>--min_live_days</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Regime gate</td><td>Reversal strategies sit out trending markets, momentum sits out mean-reverting ones</td><td><code>--no_regime_gate</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Position cap</td><td>No single name above 30% of the book (<code>conf_vol</code>)</td><td><code>--max_pos</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Cost realism</td><td><code>flat</code> (legacy) so old numbers reproduce</td><td><code>--cost_model realistic</code> for honest nets</td></tr>
</table>

<h2 id="s5">5 · Often confused with each other</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Pair</th><th>The difference</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>paper-backtest</code> vs <code>walkforward-sim</code></td><td>paper-backtest trains AND tests once (single split — optimistic); walkforward-sim never trains on the day it trades (rolling, honest). Validate with the second.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>arena-run backtest</code> vs <code>arena-run live</code></td><td>Same deterministic engine, different role: backtest = one-shot screening over a fixed window; live = incremental daily ticks persisted to arena_state/arena.db with watchdogs active.</td></tr>
<tr><td>PAUSED vs EXCLUDED</td><td>EXCLUDED failed the screening backtest (never traded live); PAUSED was trading live until the breaker tripped it. Only PAUSED can be resumed.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>predict-next</code> vs <code>arena-run live</code></td><td>predict-next is a one-off forecast + suggested allocation (nothing persisted); arena live maintains ongoing ledgers and track records.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2 id="s6">6 · Practice</h2>
